From 07a58c855aa669d8ec9d570d50198dfbf2eaf2e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:23:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Faster start: archive directories in one read, archives kept
 open

The directories of LOD, SND and VID archives were read a field at a time
through CFileInputStream with a seek between entries, so the stream
refilled its buffer for every entry: for the four big LODs about 112 MB
read and 90,000 seeks for about 380 KB of directory, 8.8 s of a 17 s
start on a Raspberry Pi. Each directory is now read in one go and parsed
from memory.

Every load() opened the archive again (1,512 opens before the main menu;
opening a file is slow on RISC OS). The archive is now opened once and
kept, and an entry is read with one seek and one read under a mutex and
handed out from memory (entries over 16 MB are still streamed).

RISC OS: the log gives each archive's index time, the number of JSON
files with their reading and parsing time, and when !Run started
(VCMI$RunAt).
---
